# DIBAY Device SSOT

Canonical docs: `docs/dibay-device-fd1-device-class-hard-lock.md` · `docs/dibay-device-fd2-window-class-hard-lock.md` · `docs/dibay-device-fd3-orientation-enforcement-hard-lock.md` · `docs/dibay-device-fd4-app-shell-navigation-hard-lock.md` · `docs/dibay-device-fd5-community-hard-lock.md`.

Historical SHA / deployment / AHEAD snapshots are **not** execution authority (TIER 4).

## DeviceClass (FD1)

- Android PRIMARY: `smallestScreenWidthDp` `>=600` → `TABLET_ANDROID` · `<600` → `PHONE_ANDROID`
- `screenLayout` = fallback only when sw unusable; sw wins on conflict
- iOS: `userInterfaceIdiom` `.phone` → `PHONE_IOS` · `.pad` → `TABLET_IPAD`
- UNKNOWN stays UNKNOWN — no fallback phone
- DeviceClass does not follow orientation or width
- Do not use 768 / 767 as DeviceClass or tablet identity
- Do not change 600dp / invent model·UA·width exceptions without a new canonical-API contradiction

## App Shell / Navigation (FD4)

- Shell identity = FD1 DeviceClass (`resolveAppShell`)
- Presentation mode = FD2 LayoutMode (not domain dual-pane)
- Navigation presentation = existing main BottomNav for PHONE / TABLET / DESKTOP / UNKNOWN
- UNKNOWN stays UNKNOWN_SAFE
- Phone cannot promote; Tablet cannot demote; Desktop narrow stays Desktop family
- `use-app-viewport-size` is measurement only
- Do not use 767/768/1024/touch/UA/orientation as Device shell identity
- Do not remount the page tree when DeviceClass or LayoutMode changes
- Do not invent a Tablet rail or restore Desktop side nav from this lock

## Community presentation (FD5)

- Community is single-page: HUB, READ, WRITE, EDIT are separate routes
- Tablet / Windows landscape use available width (`max-w-[66rem]`), not split panes
- `TABLET_ANDROID` / wide window ≠ Community master-detail
- URL `/philife/:postId` is the detail page, not a dual-pane selection
- Do not compose Community `[LIST][DETAIL]` / `[LIST][WRITE]` / `[LIST][EDIT]`
- Do not change Messenger legitimate master-detail because of Community

## Reopen

Only on a new current Production contradiction or Owner reopen. Do not reopen for historical NOT_PROVEN (iPad / Windows) alone.
